le="border-bottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="ab53bcb2-0656-42fe-b77d-3722d7cd0e33" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="9d2f9fd5-4138-4a80-9d9e-fed8eda5738d"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="5ee5fbdb-3fca-4d9d-8a42-6b22e67473c5"><p data-ref="5980df6f-e56e-4736-8843-597ecba25a34" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a C program to construct a B-Tree of a given minimum degree. First, insert a list of keys into the B-Tree and print the inorder traversal after all insertions. Then, delete a given set of keys from the B-Tree and again print the inorder traversal. Finally, search for a specific key in the current B-Tree and print whether it is found or not.</p><p data-ref="60f20a68-1389-44ad-9b25-141597fa17b4" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="5523495f-6f40-4a41-adc9-067278f01787"></p><p data-ref="08800099-ebc0-4bd0-b52d-c2885001af43" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="a80f1787-8237-43ff-904c-3c7f90c08bbb">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="a10fb254-7f9e-4fe0-b