ayed"><b style="border-bottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="0b017532-0e65-473a-a157-af74203d9437" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="5fe3ca5c-800b-4351-903c-f4ad5fc9538e"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="219f1468-4b23-4a3c-9efb-5d704887d950"><p data-ref="1f02a3bb-a6af-45b5-b618-5372bc394617" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">You are given <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.7%; position: relative;" data-ref="d6478337-5103-4b50-b0bf-8bc709b9ba6a" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="6c8f97ee-6b92-42e1-8aad-48c790f043b4"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="c5070760-40d3-46fb-a3aa-eeab9435a6d6"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="3216239f-31a5-4283-b0d6-d356ad486aa8"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="43c576f6-7fc4-4afe-af70-b0bf90de803d"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="8549f1be-a5bb-44af-9530-8bb7739a3f22"><mi data-ref="882d750e-2e55-4763-8a89-cc3738f4ed84">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> items, each with a specific weight and value. You have a knapsack with a maximum capacity <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.7%; position: relative;" data-ref="afd67337-739e-453d-851a-095b17f03157" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="3b3eef21-a0fa-4fdc-891b-57f371e855ef"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="27d8ac82-e2b2-457e-959f-35f2148d87e5"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D44A TEX-I" data-ref="77e7a103-c653-4c93-82af-aa595d342ccd"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="05f104e3-6407-4c5b-b9f9-e9623f950da1"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="12f93bf0-2b52-45c8-bf1b-a41b6e005a3e"><mi data-ref="421245a4-7d43-4131-a405-0d333233df4a">W</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>. Your goal is to select a subset of these items such that the total weight is less than or equal to <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.7%; position: relative;" data-ref="c4347ec4-7b0f-43e6-8dd8-4c0d1b3c2c55" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="1922f5cc-f0fa-4380-bd96-f727ce36ffde"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="9baae3f7-8b5e-43c5-89e1-f5ac406d4ad3"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D44A TEX-I" data-ref="91c2fb4c-6ae8-4870-b787-efcd04d38e99"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="a455cd00-db0a-4574-8e5a-735d1e9113eb"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="e75bd9cd-1f2e-48de-bdaf-8f47299c84a2"><mi data-ref="31175366-2cd6-41e3-b848-2f5d1c3a6652">W</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, and the total value is as large as possible.</p><p data-ref="7b80f71b-e058-4a0e-a4c1-eebdeefdfe3e" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="67fc09ab-0bda-4310-a789-55c3baf6a7b3"></p><p data-ref="3ff3cbbd-2f98-4d1b-8986-c2d161b3dbc9" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">This is the classic 0/1 Knapsack problem, where each item can either be included once or excluded from the knapsack.</p><p data-ref="95dc49cb-dbf8-443f-914f-dd16e5717717" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="149ad0f4-3692-4122-b1c9-ca7b51926250"></p><p data-ref="85210d6d-16ef-41e0-97e0-79c4dbb6dbeb" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="a57f6fe3-2f22-4159-a159-705bb738ccfe">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="0f557f7d-7229-4d33-8a5d-1a0ca95b9118" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="8d081fc2-0675-4738-a267-36800f3f4dc2">The first line contains an integer <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.7%; position: relative;" data-ref="cd523f75-ce6b-46a9-a044-ad04bd335d41" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="b6a828ed-d2b9-4ab1-aa4b-a4bf5c8635a5"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="85c67022-9bbe-4405-a748-13d1b1f676e5"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="3bb93a21-63e8-4633-a387-39eea55e16ab"></mjx-c