 data-ref="627d91b8-1747-4f1a-8e12-65892cf3d4d5" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="6b04a41d-cb7f-4410-a825-63d01905fad9"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="55d9b3e6-cfa9-4ef8-8c3a-41ef638ca067"><p data-ref="07e14346-9e7e-469d-8701-3e65a2cf5995" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a C program to solve the N-Queens problem using backtracking. The goal is to place <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.7%; position: relative;" data-ref="4fc7d361-e5ed-45f7-8074-1c8de3a3011c" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="657ba74a-02f5-44ff-8e3e-53dc7ee8bd8a"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="f064ab48-6658-4dbb-ba7a-9179ccb0ec4a"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D441 TEX-I" data-ref="14d90912-0feb-445b-b7b4-edfa0b2a0841"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="e4a6867f-c3c9-46ff-8271-339e705954f0"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="d1dd8c99-12ef-48f2-b51a-7e6ed4b4a1fe"><mi data-ref="ee4831df-c25a-4185-a15c-a91226491c70">N</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> queens on an <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 113.7%; position: relative;" data-ref="70818ce5-d73d-4bbe-869c-3d28bf2a0b20" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="8f3fff72-b486-4c49-85e6-c477da55acfd"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="dafa4e33-3b65-4c2f-ba72-76b66be48cbe"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D441 TEX-I" data-ref="e22f5c73-27d9-4094-bb0c-fcaad4b1bcd9"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class="mjx-n" space="3" data-ref="865407bd-3ac8-414c-b129-b10c3bc3759d"><mjx-c class="mjx